as geometry.","All three targets retain the exact same display photograph, including foreground stars and intrinsic knots; no stellar-membership separation.","Broad is an isolated finite-depth control, not a reproduction of the whole-LMC stellar-column model.","Unknown depth, thickness, and affine family tilt are authored priors; a correct front projection cannot determine them.","The 3D object uses a local laboratory frame; it is not placed in the production celestial scene.","No extinction, radiative transfer, physical gas density, or calibrated photometry is inferred."]},"approximation":{"method":"Direct XYZ emissivity samples per kpc; shared exponential opacity and optical RGB ratios; lossless full-extent RGBA8 masters. Delivery textures are area-downsampled from those PNG bytes in premultiplied display RGB, then unpremultiplied, cropped and encoded.","radialEmission":"Provided entirely by the authored emissivity sampler.","limitations":["This is display emission, not calibrated photometry; extinction is unsupported.","Shared opacity preserves column-constant chromaticity before RGBA8 quantization; varying chromaticity is a slab approximation.","Higher master resolution improves in-plane sampling only. Finite samples along each slab depth can alias high-frequency photograph detail, especially in X/Y banks.","Finite slabs, RGBA8 alpha and axis handoffs approximate a continuous volume.","Delivery downsampling averages already quantized slab coverage; lossy WebP changes RGB while alpha encoding is lossless."],"samplesPerSlab":16,"opticalWeight":1,"exposureGain":1,"emissionTransfer":"shared-opacity","sliceCounts":{"x":32,"y":32,"z":32},"slabPitchUnits":{"x":0.031249999999999997,"y":0.031249999999999997,"z":0.031249999999999997}}}}
